 "verdict": "Lean and packet still compose multiplicatively on pinned held-out data: predicted lean*packet cost factor 0.404 vs observed 0.394 (lean+packet $0.861 vs stock+raw $2.186, -61%). Both factors are weaker than on the dev set (packet ~0.81-0.83 vs 0.70; lean ~0.47-0.49 vs 0.38). Correctness: packet arms 22/22 in both profiles vs raw 21/22 (stock) and 20/22 (lean); abstention 4/4 everywhere. Zero fixture drift.",
 "caveats": [
  "n=2 reps x 11 Qs per cell; single run; small correctness gaps (1-2 trials) are not significant",
  "set is near ceiling for raw tools, so correctness separation is weak; cost is the main signal",
  "conversation questions (p09 session count, p10 abstain) dominate cost in all cells; packet saves little or costs more there (lean p10: packet $0.118 vs raw $0.091)",
  "stock profile loads the user's SessionStart hooks/MCP/skills; fixture origin URLs are dead paths so gh-based hooks see nothing live",
  "stock_raw p02 failure was an abstain after git Bash calls were refused, i.e. a permission artefact rather than a recall error",
  "the 4 pinned transcripts are the author's own overnight lane sessions; transcript subset is small (7.2MB)"
 ]
